            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi Review 0.8 (build 651)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Opening many movies at once no longer hangs the app.</b> Opening a batch of movies together from the Finder or the Dock could freeze Asobi on its opening screen for good, and nothing dropped on the window afterward would load. The more movies and the fewer processor cores, the likelier it was. Movie decoding no longer ties up the threads the rest of the app depends on.</li>
<li><b>Several files opened together become a playlist.</b> Selecting a group of files and opening them now adds them all to the playlist in order, the same as dropping them on the window, instead of showing only one.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
